<!--
  The "Hide settings" tile, on: settings are hidden, so the eye is struck out.

  The sibling of ic_hide_tile, and the same eye. The strike is not simply laid over the top:
  a tile icon is one colour, so the glyph is a hole in the gear and a dark bar over a dark
  eye would vanish into it. The bar is dilated into a halo, the halo is cut out of the eye,
  and the bar added back inside it - which leaves the even margin of gear colour on both
  sides that makes a struck-out glyph read as struck out.

  Generated by design/build_hide_tiles.py; edit the numbers there, not this file.
-->
